hermes v2026.9.14 (0.21.3): with the Camofox backend the agent has no way
through an image CAPTCHA (reCAPTCHA grid, hCaptcha, GeeTest, ...).

Symptom: a page gated by a captcha challenge stops the agent. browser_vision
can describe the grid, but the agent's clicks by ref cannot reach the tiles
inside the challenge's cross-origin frame, and its model is no captcha reader.

Upstream: neither hermes-agent (main 848fc0ad) nor camofox-browser (v1.18.1)
has a captcha solver hook; camofox-browser's plugin system can carry one.
hyperconfig's camofox-browser has it (pkgs/camofox-browser/captcha-plugin:
POST /tabs/<id>/solve-captcha, CaptchaKraken on the tab's live page against a
self-hosted model).

Fix: one tool, browser_solve_captcha, offered only in Camofox mode and not
routed to an extension controller. It asks the server to solve the captcha on
the session's own tab and returns status (solved, no_captcha, failed with the
solver's reason), vendor, rounds and seconds, plus what to do next. It waits
180 s: the server ends a solve after 120 s by closing the tab, after up to
35 s of waiting for the tab's lock. A closed tab (404/410) is forgotten so the
next browser_navigate opens a new one; a server without the route says so.

The new test fails before this change: tools.browser_camofox has no
camofox_solve_captcha.

